## Codebase Patterns

Consolidated, reusable knowledge. Re-read in full every session -- keep
it tight.

- **No lint script.** `npm run lint` does not exist. The lint+dep gate
  is `npm test`, which runs `standard && depcheck`. There is no unit
  test runner yet; one arrives in US-019.
- **Babel JSX config lives in the `babel` key of `package.json`**, not
  a `.babelrc`. It is `@babel/plugin-transform-react-jsx` with
  `useBuiltIns: true`. Reuse those exact options anywhere JSX has to be
  compiled.
- **`npm start` = `npm run build && electron --no-sandbox .`** where
  `npm run build` is `babel src --out-dir build`. The Babel build must
  keep working at every commit (FR-2), independently of Vite.
- **Verifying the app launches non-interactively:** run
  `npx electron --no-sandbox .` in the background, sleep ~12s, check
  the process is alive and that the log shows `'Main Window'` and
  `init: <time>`. Always kill the process afterwards. This is a launch
  check only -- it is NOT the six-step manual smoke test.
- **Vite 8 is Rolldown-based, not Rollup/esbuild.** Two consequences
  that will keep mattering: it handles CommonJS natively (no
  `@rollup/plugin-commonjs`, no CJS resolve errors), and Node builtins
  are externalized to throwing browser stubs with a *warning*, not an
  error. A green Vite build therefore proves very little on its own --
  check the warning stream, not just the exit code.
- **`electron` resolves silently to the wrong module.** Bundlers
  resolve `require('electron')` to `node_modules/electron/index.js`,
  the npm CLI helper that exports a path string, not the runtime API.
  No warning is emitted. Anything relying on `electron.ipcRenderer`
  will be `undefined` at runtime while the build reports success.
- **`docs/vite-baseline.md`** is the measured inventory of what Vite
  cannot handle in the renderer, grouped by cause. Consult it before
  guessing at scope for any Phase 1 story.

